                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Sometimes it's hard to make new friends. Sometimes it's hard to even talk to someone. And how it must be hard when you're all alone, you don't know who you are and you have a movie projector instead of your face.\n\nProjector Face is essentially a traditional point & click adventure game true to the concept of Adventure Game Studio engine. However it brings some unique concepts to its genre. The hero, a sort of a projector-man, decides to leave his solitude and comes into town to look for new friends … for anyone to speak with. Soon he discovers it’s hard to speak with someone, because ... in fact, he can’t speak at all. And the only way how to say something is to play a movie from his projector. It’s not so easy though, he needs to find a perfect spot to show the movie on and collect all movie pieces to stick it together. In this moment the game has elements of hidden object, because the pieces of film are sometimes quite hidden. Playing the entire movie can be done in certain places only and without this show for local children, which is always really surprising for them, game can’t proceed.\n\nAll is followed by a very nice stylized hand-drawn graphics, and although the authors suggest that a simple character animation is caused by a low budget, I think it fits the game well. Story is narrated by illustrated frames like from the silent film era with nice background music during play.\n\nOverall I must say that despite its very short playing time I enjoyed playing the game and generally this topic makes you think more about movies, art and how it communicates with us.",
